<title>UK: TransCo UK gas forecasts for March 4.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas forecasts for March 4.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas consumption for the period March 2-4.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Mar 2 (actual) 250 mcm, 58 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 3 (forecast) 287 mcm, 67 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 4 (forecast) 290 mcm, 68 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Mar 2 (actual) 7.5 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.3 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 3 (forecast) 5.8 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.4 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 4 (forecast) 7.7 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.4 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption on Monday and the probability of interruption across the network on Tuesday is low.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
